10.3,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":3.5030996004959363,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":false,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":11.0,"_gate_accruals":-0.013117516096034659,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":17.4,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.12344916519736622,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":79.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.00022225738691362962,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":99.7,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.04964563074475174,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":24.8,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.3348313331515278,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":44.2,"_gate_incr_roic":0.06260040834393324,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":37.5,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.01014330345398931,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":36.7,"_gate_pool_share":-0.08350411992431805,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":6.6,"_gate_rev_durability":0.025409037690064418,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":37.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.061412720830675394,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.0010806012206555527,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":51.1,"_gate_fund_growth":0.008783618135258856,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":8.8,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02935425286045695,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":43.7,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0030836438391365797,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":94.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.030639999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":20.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Greif, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, produces and sells industrial packaging products and services worldwide. It operates in four segments: Customized Polymer Solutions; Durable Metal Solutions; Sustainable Fiber Solutions; and Integrated Solutions. The Customized Polymer Solutions segment produces and sells polymer-based packaging products, such as plastic drums, rigid intermediate bulk containers, and small plastics for chemicals, food and beverage, agricultural, pharmaceutical, and mineral products industries. The Durable Metal Solutions segment offers metal-based packaging products, including various steel drums for the chemicals, petroleum, agriculture, and paints and coatings industries. The Sustainable Fiber Solutions segment provides fiber-based packaging products comprising fibre drums, uncoated recycled board, coated recycled board, tubes and cores, and specialty partitions made from uncoated recycled board and coated recycled board to packaging, automotive, construction, food and beverage, and building products industries. The Integrated Solutions segment offers complimentary packaging products, such as paints, linings, and closure systems for industrial packaging products and related services. The company manufactures and sells rigid industrial packaging products, such as steel, fibre and plastic drums, rigid intermediate bulk containers, jerrycans and other small plastics, closure systems for industrial packaging products, water bottles, and remanufactured and reconditioned industrial containers, as well as offers container life cycle management, logistics, warehousing, and other packaging services. It also purchases and sells recycled fiber; and produces and sells adhesives. The company was formerly known as Greif Bros. Corporation and changed its name to Greif, Inc. in 2001. Greif, Inc. was founded in 1877 and is headquartered in Delaware, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ole G. Rosgaard | President, CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $3.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Greif Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $4.1B market cap on $5.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 7% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 20% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $170M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.32\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 3.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $8.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 47% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 28% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","30 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Greif (GEF) Stock Looks Reasonable As Cost Savings Goals Expand","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-gef/greif/news/greif-gef-stock-looks-reasonable-as-cost-savings-goals-expan","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793965105.513,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.956,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(GEF.B) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/39/GEF.B_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets_110526015802_1793861882.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793861882.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Greif Inc (GEF) (Q4 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Adjusted EPS Surges 75% as Cost Savings and ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/greif-inc-gef-q4-2026-010704249.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793840824.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Greif (GEF) Q4 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"fool.com","link":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/04/grei